# Knowbase — Cursor / agent rules (compat)

This file mirrors project guidance for tools that read `.cursorrules`.
Canonical, scoped rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. Also see `CLAUDE.md` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.

## Product
Knowbase: exam-prep knowledge base. Flow: audio lecture → STT → corpus (+ materials) → conspect → Q&A with citations. No concept map.

## Stack
Java 17, Spring Boot 3.4, SQLite + JdbcTemplate, JWT, OpenRouter (chat + Whisper). Frontend: Vite + vanilla JS. API :8081, UI :5173.

## Architecture
`com.ailab.<feature>` package-by-feature. Controller → Service → Repository. Always `CourseService.requireOwned(courseId)` for course data. Errors → `{ "error": "..." }` (Russian messages). JSON camelCase maps.

## Good examples (copy these shapes)

### 1) Ownership + validation (CourseService)
```java
public CourseRepository.CourseRow requireOwned(String courseId) {
    String userId = AuthContext.requireUserId();
    CourseRepository.CourseRow course = courses.findById(courseId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalArgumentException("Курс не найден"));
    if (!course.userId().equals(userId)) {
        throw new SecurityException("Нет доступа к курсу");
    }
    return course;
}
```

### 2) Thin controller + nested record (CourseController)
```java
public record CreateCourseRequest(String title, String subject) {}

@PostMapping
public Map<String, Object> create(@RequestBody CreateCourseRequest request) {
    return courseService.create(request.title(), request.subject());
}
```

### 3) Repository SQL + SQLite Long helper (ChunkRepository)
```java
jdbc.update("""
    INSERT INTO chunks(id, lecture_id, course_id, ordinal, text, start_ms, end_ms)
    VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?,?)
    """, row.id(), row.lectureId(), row.courseId(), row.ordinal(), row.text(),
    row.startMs(), row.endMs());
// use toLong(rs.getObject("start_ms")) when reading nullable longs
```

### 4) Frontend API helper (js/api.js)
```js
export async function api(path, options = {}) {
  const headers = { ...(options.headers || {}) };
  const token = getToken();
  if (token) headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  // ... parse JSON, throw Error(data.error) on !res.ok
}
```

### 5) Global API errors (ApiExceptionHandler)
```java
@ExceptionHandler(IllegalArgumentException.class)
public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> badRequest(IllegalArgumentException ex) {
    return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body(Map.of("error", ex.getMessage()));
}
```

## Antipatterns
1. SQL or business logic in controllers / HTML
2. Skipping ownership checks
3. Hardcoded secrets / committing `application-local.yml`
4. `console.log` of auth tokens; noisy debug in committed UI
5. New stacks (React, JPA entities for everything) without request
6. Concept-map endpoints or tables

## Typical new endpoint file set
1. Optional `*Repository` methods (SQL only here; share with feature service — no dual access)
2. **Dedicated** aggregate `*Service` (keep `CourseService` CRUD-only): `requireOwned` → work → `LinkedHashMap` response
3. Mapping on `CourseAiController` for `/api/courses/{courseId}/...`
4. `SecurityException` → 403 in `ApiExceptionHandler`
5. Update README API table
6. Materials = `lectures.source_type = MATERIAL`

## Config layers
- **Global** (user Cursor rules): personal prefs, language, commit style
- **Local** (this repo `.cursor/rules`): stack & patterns — take precedence
- **Skill** `.cursor/skills/add-course-endpoint`: checklist for course APIs
- **Subagents**: explore / shell / one-shot implementers for isolated tasks
